WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:02.668
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.050
- How can I know that
you're being honest with me,

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.030
and did you lie to any of us?

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.740
- I don't think I've lied to anybody.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:17.910
I guess, I could be lying to you.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.370
- [Female Speaker] If
you were alone in a room

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.470
with a diagnosed sociopath,

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.790
what would you ask?

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.080
- Have you ever been in love?

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.270
- What does empathy look like for you?

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:28.590
- Have you ever felt guilt?

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.246
- That's like a complicate question.

00:00:30.246 --> 00:00:32.829
(upbeat music)

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.770
- How are you doing?

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:35.603
- Pretty good.

00:00:35.603 --> 00:00:36.436
- Okay, that's good.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.320
- What's your name?

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.947
- Greg.

00:00:38.947 --> 00:00:40.676
- All right, nice to meet
you, nice to meet you.

00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:43.043
- What age were you diagnosed?

00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:45.810
- I think I was around 21, 22.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.040
- How old are you?

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.720
- I am 33.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.840
- What's your definition of a sociopath?

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.845
- A sociopath to me is someone who has

00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:56.730
no regard for themselves
or for other people.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.720
You're very impulsive, very
irresponsible, reckless,

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.160
basically like a child.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.490
- Were you surprised
when you got diagnosed?

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.260
- I don't think surprised
is the right word.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.580
I think relieved, like I
had felt out of control.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.250
And, I didn't understand why I was doing

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:15.630
what I was doing for a long time.

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:18.780
So, knowing that there
was an actual reason

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.090
behind why I was doing these things,

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.494
it was really like kind of freeing in way.

00:01:23.494 --> 00:01:26.307
- What made you think you was a sociopath?

00:01:26.307 --> 00:01:29.688
- Waking up in prison was
probably my first clue.

00:01:29.688 --> 00:01:32.640
- Do you mind me asking what
led you to go to prison?

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.830
- I've committed several crimes.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:38.250
I was using drugs and
selling to support my habit.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.830
I also have like many retail thefts.

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:44.160
- How long ago did you
commit those crimes?

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.060
- The last time I committed
any crimes was 2011.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.850
- And then, you haven't
committed any crime since then?

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.740
- I wouldn't say I haven't
committed any crimes.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.870
I haven't committed any
major crimes since then.

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.240
Actually, I don't even
drive recklessly anymore

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:58.080
like I used to.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.490
I stopped stealing.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.670
Now that I say it, I don't
know if I've been doing crimes.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.200
I think I changed my ways.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.750
- What made you make the
decision to change your life?

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:08.700
- Not wanting to go back to prison.

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:12.787
It was one of the worst
experiences of my life.

00:02:12.787 --> 00:02:17.062
- What do you think people
most often misunderstand

00:02:17.062 --> 00:02:19.440
about being a sociopath?

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.970
- Personally, I think
that the stereotype is

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:27.030
that they're incredibly
violent and just malicious

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.110
just to be mean.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.910
And like, just for it's own sake.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:33.780
At least for me, that's
not how it presents.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.794
More often then not, people

00:02:35.794 --> 00:02:38.917
with antisocial personality
disorder, sociopaths,

00:02:38.917 --> 00:02:41.580
they're just irresponsible,
impulsive people.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.176
That can lead to you being a little bit

00:02:44.176 --> 00:02:47.970
aggressive and irritable, but
the myth that they're violent

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:51.660
and just out of control monsters is blown

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:52.946
way out of proportion.

00:02:52.946 --> 00:02:56.118
- Have you ever manipulated
someone to benefit you?

00:02:56.118 --> 00:02:57.690
- Yeah, of course.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:01.770
I feel like everyone
manipulates other people

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:02.640
to an extent.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.652
We're all trying to get something out

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:08.610
of any given relationship.

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:12.510
- Okay, I haven't really
thought of it that way.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:15.450
For me, it's more like mutual respect

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.650
and wanting to do others

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:18.323
for people to make them feel better.

00:03:18.323 --> 00:03:20.520
- Yeah, I see what you men.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:23.850
I look at all of my relationships
as very transactional.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:28.080
And, it's just kind of the way
that I engage with the world.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.110
- What are some things that piss you off?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:33.210
- When people can't admit they're wrong

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.480
or made a mistake, that
drives me absolutely crazy.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.700
And, I think that's just
because I used to do

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:39.570
that same thing.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:42.000
I used to not ever admit that I was wrong.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.190
- What does empathy look like for you

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:46.410
if you have empathy at all?

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.720
- So, I call it cognitive empathy.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.734
It's just me making sure that put myself

00:03:51.734 --> 00:03:55.950
in someone else's shoes,
like intentionally.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.200
My first response in
any given situation is

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.160
never empathy.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:03.870
It's usually some like
logical like solution

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:04.740
to the problem.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:07.290
When a lot of the times,
that's not what people need.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.598
They need you to listen
and just be there for them.

00:04:10.598 --> 00:04:13.560
- Have you ever felt guilt or remorse?

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.427
Is that something that you feel?

00:04:15.427 --> 00:04:17.820
- That's like a complicated question.

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.370
So, at the time, I didn't feel bad

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.660
about anything that I did.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.400
I really didn't have a care in the world.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.660
Once I move on from it,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.780
like in my head, it's over to me.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:31.560
Which isn't great when you
cheated on your partner,

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:33.720
and then, they don't forget about that.

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:34.553
- Yeah.

00:04:34.553 --> 00:04:36.180
- But, I would. I regret it now,

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.760
because I don't like that
I put people through that.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:41.160
And, I don't like that I hurt them,.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.570
But that's now.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.710
That wasn't then.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:47.232
- I wanted to ask you what
your childhood was like.

00:04:47.232 --> 00:04:50.670
- Part of the problem is,
like I don't store memories

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:53.760
very well, so I don't necessarily remember

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.140
much of my childhood.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:59.280
- Is that a condition associated
with being a sociopath?

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:02.670
- From what I've gathered, memory is tied

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:04.680
to emotion fairly strongly.

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.640
The way that I experience
emotions is not quite as deep

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.630
as other people.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:14.280
So, the emotional tie to like memories is

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.960
that makes them stick in your brain

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.120
doesn't really happen for me that often.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.610
- Did you tell your parents
about your diagnosis

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:21.600
right away?

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:22.770
- No, actually, I didn't.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:26.198
I've only actually
mentioned it to my parents

00:05:26.198 --> 00:05:27.810
like one time.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:29.790
When I told them, they didn't believe me.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.410
They're like, "That's
not the Greg I knew."

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.920
And, I guess it just speaks
to how fooled I had them.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:37.989
They just didn't believe that
I was capable of those things.

00:05:37.989 --> 00:05:39.494
- Have you ever been in love,

00:05:39.494 --> 00:05:40.964
and do you feel love?

00:05:40.964 --> 00:05:42.480
- I think so.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.620
Like, I do experience emotions and love

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.180
and connection and closeness.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.150
It's just maybe not to the depth

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:54.120
or like breadth of some other people.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.400
- Who would you say is
your favorite person

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.230
in your life right now?

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:02.040
- Probably my son, followed
very shortly after that

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.090
by my partner.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:08.090
He's one of the main reasons
that I've gotten better.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.500
- And, your diagnosis hasn't affected

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.354
your parenting in any way?

00:06:12.354 --> 00:06:15.327
- Wanting to be the best
dad I can for him is

00:06:15.327 --> 00:06:17.970
like a huge motivating factor for me,

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:19.830
'cause, I don't want him to live

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:21.030
the same life I've lived.

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:24.420
There's a huge genetic
component to sociopathy.

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:27.540
And, the other half of
that is your environment.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.156
So, I have to do everything I can

00:06:29.156 --> 00:06:32.250
with his environment to
overcome his genetics.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:36.132
- How did you feel when
you first met your wife?

00:06:36.132 --> 00:06:39.150
- It's always been her,

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.430
even though there was a period of time

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.470
when I was really not a good boyfriend.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.390
I was not a good partner.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:47.250
I don't deserve to still have her,

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.010
but she stuck it out and knew

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:55.010
that there was a person
inside of that version of Greg

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.640
that was better.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.380
- Do you go to therapy?

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:00.030
- I have gone to therapy in the past.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.740
At the time I was in prison,

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:05.910
I did have what's called
a therapeutic community.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:08.460
And, they do cognitive behavioral therapy.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.490
And, when I left prison,
I didn't continue.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.800
Nowadays it's more like self led.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:16.380
Like I do self exploration.

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.500
And, with my partner,
we kind of explore it

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.610
if something happens.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.620
She'll gently let me know.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.600
It feels like and accusation,

00:07:24.600 --> 00:07:26.220
like you're doing something wrong.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.360
I'll shut down.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.980
I don't like being told what to do.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.840
So, a lot of the times, I don't know,

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.970
I require gentle guidance.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:35.070
- Is that you saying, like you think

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:40.070
you've learned how to cope
with being a sociopath?

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.144
- So, the way I look at it is

00:07:42.144 --> 00:07:47.144
that I've learned how
to not destroy my life

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:48.450
by accident.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:53.010
I can manage to stop those
thoughts and impulses

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:56.400
before they lead to actions.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:59.520
- How can I know that
you're being honest with me,

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.353
and did you lie to any of us?

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:03.870
- I don't think I've lied to anybody.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.400
I guess I could be lying to you,

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:10.050
but it doesn't serve me to lie to you

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.075
or to most people.

00:08:12.075 --> 00:08:15.502
I'm here to like share my
actual lived experience.

00:08:15.502 --> 00:08:17.010
I'm not gonna like to you about it.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.847
- [Female Speaker] And, if
you'd like this chance to meet

00:08:20.847 --> 00:08:23.373
face to face, it's the moment to do it.

00:08:25.057 --> 00:08:25.890
- Hi.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:26.723
- Hi.

00:08:26.723 --> 00:08:27.556
- Nice to meet you.

00:08:27.556 --> 00:08:28.452
- Nice to meet you.

00:08:28.452 --> 00:08:29.443
- Hi. Sorry.

00:08:29.443 --> 00:08:30.327
- You're good.

00:08:30.327 --> 00:08:31.470
- Nice to meet you.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:32.303
- Likewise.

00:08:32.303 --> 00:08:33.557
- Hey, how are you doing?

00:08:33.557 --> 00:08:34.390
- Greg.

00:08:34.390 --> 00:08:35.223
- Nathan. Nice to meet you, Greg.

00:08:35.223 --> 00:08:36.379
- Likewise.

00:08:36.379 --> 00:08:37.590
- I can put a face to
you. So, that's cool.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.430
- It's a pretty face.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:39.788
- It is.

00:08:39.788 --> 00:08:40.621
- Nice to meet you.

00:08:40.621 --> 00:08:41.580
- Likewise.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.413
Those were great questions. Thank you.

00:08:42.413 --> 00:08:43.246
- Thank you.

